WEBVTT

00:00:00.043 --> 00:00:01.044 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Builder.

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
GridBot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.074 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Introduction.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.489 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.061 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.164 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.448 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is high risk; you could

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:20.139 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lose all the money you put in.

00:00:20.659 --> 00:00:22.724 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:22.724 --> 00:00:24.434 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
indicator of future results.

00:00:25.484 --> 00:00:27.540 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The prices are public historical

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.302 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:29.822 --> 00:00:31.889 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A close is the last price of the day.

00:00:33.044 --> 00:00:34.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:00:35.942 --> 00:00:37.841 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end of this series you will

00:00:37.841 --> 00:00:40.076 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
understand what a grid bot does, when it

00:00:40.076 --> 00:00:42.311 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
can capture bounces, and where it loses.

00:00:42.772 --> 00:00:44.783 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will know how to plan one, test

00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:46.682 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it on paper, run it, check it, and

00:00:46.682 --> 00:00:48.730 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
change the capital you give to bots

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
only under written risk rules.

00:00:51.111 --> 00:00:52.508 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is education, not

00:00:52.508 --> 00:00:53.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a promise of results.

00:00:54.348 --> 00:00:55.958 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price often moves sideways,

00:00:55.958 --> 00:00:57.709 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bouncing between the same top

00:00:57.709 --> 00:00:59.459 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and bottom instead of leaving.

00:00:59.979 --> 00:01:01.557 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid is a ladder of limit

00:01:01.557 --> 00:01:03.510 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders built for that bouncing.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.886 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When price runs one way and stays

00:01:05.886 --> 00:01:08.009 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
there, the bot has nothing left to do.

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.271 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
By the end you will know

00:01:10.271 --> 00:01:11.556 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
what a grid bot places.

00:01:12.684 --> 00:01:14.763 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will see that idea on

00:01:14.763 --> 00:01:16.738 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
one real path from 2023.

00:01:17.938 --> 00:01:19.446 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You will be able to say the

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:20.899 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stop rule in one sentence.

00:01:21.853 --> 00:01:23.699 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
When a chart says Example, it

00:01:23.699 --> 00:01:25.545 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
means a real past price used

00:01:25.545 --> 00:01:27.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
as an example, not a forecast.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.951 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto is digital money, such as bitcoin.

00:01:31.471 --> 00:01:33.147 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You do not need to have bought

00:01:33.147 --> 00:01:34.432 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
any before this lesson.

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:36.778 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An exchange is the website or app

00:01:36.778 --> 00:01:39.110 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
where you swap Australian dollars for

00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.150 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
crypto, and crypto back to dollars.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.346 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course does not name one,

00:01:43.346 --> 00:01:45.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it does not send an order.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.331 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Cash is money you can spend.

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:49.632 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here that means dollars, or a coin

00:01:49.632 --> 00:01:51.755 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that is meant to stay near one dollar.

00:01:52.063 --> 00:01:54.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Coin is the crypto, such as bitcoin.

00:01:55.304 --> 00:01:57.650 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order is an instruction to buy or sell.

00:01:58.103 --> 00:01:59.910 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy order swaps cash for coin.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.794 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell order swaps coin back to cash, and

00:02:02.794 --> 00:02:05.158 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you can only sell coin you already hold.

00:02:06.208 --> 00:02:07.978 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot is software that places

00:02:07.978 --> 00:02:09.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and refills orders for you.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:12.484 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

00:02:12.484 --> 00:02:14.613 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on lines below the price and sell

00:02:14.613 --> 00:02:16.741 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
orders on lines above it, inside a

00:02:16.741 --> 00:02:18.475 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
top and a bottom you choose.

00:02:18.995 --> 00:02:20.671 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The space between your top and

00:02:20.671 --> 00:02:22.403 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your bottom is called the band.

00:02:22.512 --> 00:02:24.618 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:02:24.618 --> 00:02:26.567 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
starts with part cash and part

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.516 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, and that is a description,

00:02:28.516 --> 00:02:30.388 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
not advice about what to hold.

00:02:31.438 --> 00:02:33.144 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A limit order is an order that

00:02:33.144 --> 00:02:34.708 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waits at a price you choose.

00:02:35.228 --> 00:02:36.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not chase the price.

00:02:37.211 --> 00:02:38.775 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Chasing the price would mean

00:02:38.775 --> 00:02:40.228 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
moving the order to follow

00:02:40.228 --> 00:02:41.792 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wherever the price has gone.

00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:44.717 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
An order fills when the price reaches

00:02:44.717 --> 00:02:46.449 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
its line and the trade happens.

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Until then, the order is only waiting.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:52.122 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

00:02:52.263 --> 00:02:54.609 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

00:02:54.885 --> 00:02:57.176 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A rung is one price where an order waits.

00:02:57.583 --> 00:02:59.762 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The gap is the space between two rungs.

00:03:00.051 --> 00:03:02.095 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The ladder is the analogy, and the

00:03:02.095 --> 00:03:04.367 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
chart beside it is the real past path.

00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.828 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top rung

00:03:06.828 --> 00:03:07.957 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the bottom rung.

00:03:08.477 --> 00:03:10.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the rungs between them.

00:03:10.949 --> 00:03:13.240 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is the written rule for leaving.

00:03:14.089 --> 00:03:15.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The range is the top line and the

00:03:15.933 --> 00:03:17.776 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom line, taken from the path.

00:03:18.255 --> 00:03:21.479 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The chart is bitcoin's real daily

00:03:21.479 --> 00:03:25.049 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes from 19 July to 16 October 2023.

00:03:25.569 --> 00:03:27.022 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Every close in this window

00:03:27.022 --> 00:03:28.753 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
stayed between those two lines.

00:03:29.539 --> 00:03:32.131 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:03:32.131 --> 00:03:34.803 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:03:35.323 --> 00:03:37.550 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.777 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the top line minus the bottom

00:03:39.777 --> 00:03:41.262 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
line, divided by six.

00:03:41.782 --> 00:03:43.117 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It is one step between

00:03:43.117 --> 00:03:44.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines, not the whole band.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.959 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Seven lines make those six gaps.

00:03:47.479 --> 00:03:49.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The levels are the prices on the

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:50.943 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
rungs where limit orders wait.

00:03:51.929 --> 00:03:54.220 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Buy orders wait on lines below the price.

00:03:54.656 --> 00:03:56.611 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Sell orders wait on lines above it.

00:03:57.092 --> 00:03:59.592 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Each fill changes what you hold: a buy

00:03:59.592 --> 00:04:02.257 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fill adds coin, and a sell fill adds cash.

00:04:02.777 --> 00:04:03.894 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You choose the band,

00:04:03.894 --> 00:04:05.179 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the gaps and the money.

00:04:05.464 --> 00:04:06.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot places each order.

00:04:07.923 --> 00:04:09.716 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
After a fill, the bot places the

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:11.437 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
opposite order one rung away.

00:04:11.957 --> 00:04:14.136 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A buy fill gets a sell one rung higher.

00:04:14.522 --> 00:04:16.751 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A sell fill gets a buy one rung lower.

00:04:17.271 --> 00:04:18.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You still write the stop, and

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:20.567 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you act when that rule is met.

00:04:20.799 --> 00:04:23.034 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop for you

00:04:23.034 --> 00:04:25.157 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on, and

00:04:25.157 --> 00:04:27.224 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you write which one before you start.

00:04:27.958 --> 00:04:29.299 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Think of a market stall.

00:04:29.731 --> 00:04:31.845 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stallholder buys stock a little

00:04:31.845 --> 00:04:33.959 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cheaper and sells it a little dearer,

00:04:33.959 --> 00:04:35.579 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and pays a fee on every sale.

00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:37.757 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid can do that while price

00:04:37.757 --> 00:04:39.197 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bounces inside the band.

00:04:39.717 --> 00:04:42.238 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bounce means price moves down and back

00:04:42.238 --> 00:04:44.607 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
up, or up and back down, and stays inside.

00:04:45.127 --> 00:04:47.363 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
One buy at a lower line and the later

00:04:47.363 --> 00:04:49.445 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sell of that same coin is one pair.

00:04:49.965 --> 00:04:52.299 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On these daily closes, the summer window

00:04:52.299 --> 00:04:54.703 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
finished only three pairs one rung apart.

00:04:55.223 --> 00:04:56.955 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The sell line is higher, so the

00:04:56.955 --> 00:04:58.798 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
cash that comes back is more than

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.754 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the cash that left, before the fee.

00:05:01.047 --> 00:05:02.500 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A fee is what the exchange

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.064 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
charges when an order fills.

00:05:04.245 --> 00:05:05.865 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fee comes out of the gap.

00:05:06.092 --> 00:05:07.824 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the fees are larger than the

00:05:07.824 --> 00:05:09.388 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
gap, the pair keeps nothing.

00:05:09.569 --> 00:05:10.812 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is not a promise.

00:05:11.332 --> 00:05:13.136 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair finishes only if price

00:05:13.136 --> 00:05:15.009 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
does bounce and both orders fill.

00:05:16.059 --> 00:05:17.288 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the

00:05:17.288 --> 00:05:18.517 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
last price of the day.

00:05:18.938 --> 00:05:20.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Crypto trades all day, so the

00:05:20.737 --> 00:05:22.146 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
day is cut at a set time.

00:05:22.666 --> 00:05:25.190 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The daily close is the end of each

00:05:25.190 --> 00:05:27.621 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
UTC day, 11am in Sydney in summer.

00:05:28.141 --> 00:05:30.124 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This is a simple candle that shows

00:05:30.124 --> 00:05:31.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the day's high, low and close.

00:05:32.274 --> 00:05:34.203 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Traders call it a candle because

00:05:34.203 --> 00:05:36.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the full version has a thick body

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:37.865 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and a thin wick, like a candle.

00:05:38.296 --> 00:05:39.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here we only need the high,

00:05:39.804 --> 00:05:41.033 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the low and the close.

00:05:41.368 --> 00:05:44.547 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This candle is 19 July 2023.

00:05:45.067 --> 00:05:46.296 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high, the low, and

00:05:46.296 --> 00:05:47.581 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the close are labelled.

00:05:48.474 --> 00:05:50.603 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The example is Bitcoin's public

00:05:50.603 --> 00:05:52.259 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
daily price in US dollars.

00:05:52.779 --> 00:05:55.978 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

00:05:55.978 --> 00:05:58.921 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023, every one of those days

00:05:58.921 --> 00:06:01.352 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closed inside the band.

00:06:01.872 --> 00:06:03.545 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The close crossed the seven

00:06:03.545 --> 00:06:05.291 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lines 28 times in that window.

00:06:05.811 --> 00:06:08.122 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The count is an example, not a forecast.

00:06:08.642 --> 00:06:10.430 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
We do not need to read each day.

00:06:10.696 --> 00:06:12.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The shape is the lesson,

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:13.452 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and it is marked Example.

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:16.729 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Worked check: 19 July

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:19.809 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
2023 to 16 October 2023.

00:06:20.329 --> 00:06:21.837 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The low is the bottom line.

00:06:22.317 --> 00:06:23.784 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The high is the top line.

00:06:24.304 --> 00:06:26.148 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Nothing on this card is an order.

00:06:27.111 --> 00:06:30.045 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those 28 crossings are not 28 results.

00:06:30.565 --> 00:06:32.767 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A crossing only means the close moved

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.834 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
from one side of a line to the other.

00:06:35.276 --> 00:06:36.987 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A pair is finished only when a

00:06:36.987 --> 00:06:38.841 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
buy and its later sell have both

00:06:38.841 --> 00:06:40.573 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled, and only after the fee.

00:06:41.072 --> 00:06:42.971 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The price can cross many lines and

00:06:42.971 --> 00:06:44.871 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
still leave you holding coin if it

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:46.491 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
walks out through the bottom.

00:06:47.028 --> 00:06:50.009 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In this example a buy waiting at the

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:53.298 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower of these two lines was reached on

00:06:53.298 --> 00:06:56.279 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
17 August 2023, and the sell one line

00:06:56.279 --> 00:06:59.260 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above was reached on 29 August 2023.

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:01.568 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The card shows the gap, then the

00:07:01.568 --> 00:07:03.132 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
two fees, then what is left.

00:07:03.441 --> 00:07:05.564 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is about eight and a half dollars

00:07:05.564 --> 00:07:07.296 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
after fees, for one small pair.

00:07:07.692 --> 00:07:09.591 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It happens only if the price comes

00:07:09.591 --> 00:07:11.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
back up through the sell line.

00:07:11.371 --> 00:07:13.103 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If the price leaves through the

00:07:13.103 --> 00:07:14.891 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, you still hold the coin,

00:07:14.891 --> 00:07:16.455 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the pair never finishes.

00:07:16.647 --> 00:07:18.435 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This card is not money you made.

00:07:25.363 --> 00:07:27.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Now watch what you hold when the

00:07:27.151 --> 00:07:29.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
price leaves the band and stays out.

00:07:29.425 --> 00:07:31.045 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Above the band the sells have

00:07:31.045 --> 00:07:32.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding cash,

00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:34.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with nothing left to sell.

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.254 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Below the band the buys have

00:07:36.254 --> 00:07:37.707 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you are holding

00:07:37.707 --> 00:07:39.439 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
coin, with nothing left to buy.

00:07:39.721 --> 00:07:41.113 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That is why the way down

00:07:41.113 --> 00:07:42.871 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
matters most: every buy fills,

00:07:42.871 --> 00:07:44.630 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you are left holding coin.

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.915 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Here is that stop rule on the real path.

00:07:49.335 --> 00:07:51.696 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It triggers if a daily close is outside

00:07:51.696 --> 00:07:53.983 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the band, through the top or the bottom,

00:07:53.983 --> 00:07:56.491 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and the next daily close is still outside.

00:07:57.011 --> 00:07:58.464 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then the idea is finished.

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:00.938 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot, which cancels the

00:08:00.938 --> 00:08:02.807 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
waiting orders, and do what you

00:08:02.807 --> 00:08:04.901 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
wrote: keep the coin or swap to cash.

00:08:05.421 --> 00:08:07.403 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A bot's automatic stop is a price

00:08:07.403 --> 00:08:09.091 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
that can fire during the day.

00:08:09.611 --> 00:08:11.310 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This course uses the two daily

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.146 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
closes, unless your written plan

00:08:13.146 --> 00:08:14.934 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
says you turned on a price stop.

00:08:15.365 --> 00:08:16.985 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The stop is your written rule

00:08:16.985 --> 00:08:18.438 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
for when you stop the bot.

00:08:18.671 --> 00:08:20.804 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On 23 October 2023 the close

00:08:20.804 --> 00:08:23.216 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
finished above the top line, and

00:08:23.216 --> 00:08:25.536 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day was still above it.

00:08:30.586 --> 00:08:32.039 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the top, the sells

00:08:32.039 --> 00:08:33.714 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
have filled and you hold cash.

00:08:33.823 --> 00:08:35.667 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Through the bottom, the buys have

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:37.510 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
filled and you hold coin that you

00:08:37.510 --> 00:08:39.521 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bought above where the price is now.

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:41.333 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
That loss can keep growing

00:08:41.333 --> 00:08:42.450 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
until the stop acts.

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.599 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot either way, then

00:08:44.599 --> 00:08:46.163 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you follow the written rule.

00:08:46.272 --> 00:08:48.060 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The bot does not decide the stop

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:49.959 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unless you turned that setting on.

00:08:50.232 --> 00:08:52.355 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
EXAMPLE, made up: three buys fill

00:08:52.355 --> 00:08:54.151 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
on the way down, and you paid

00:08:54.151 --> 00:08:56.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
about 800 dollars for that coin.

00:08:56.795 --> 00:08:58.627 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A little below the band

00:08:58.627 --> 00:09:00.266 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
it is worth about 720.

00:09:00.786 --> 00:09:02.482 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You are down about 80 dollars

00:09:02.482 --> 00:09:04.248 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
before fees, and the loss keeps

00:09:04.248 --> 00:09:05.944 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
growing until your stop acts.

00:09:06.994 --> 00:09:08.569 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A common mistake is thinking

00:09:08.569 --> 00:09:10.077 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot predicts the price.

00:09:10.866 --> 00:09:11.616 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It does not.

00:09:12.183 --> 00:09:12.965 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
It only waits.

00:09:13.334 --> 00:09:14.842 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Another mistake is starting

00:09:14.842 --> 00:09:16.016 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with no written stop.

00:09:16.431 --> 00:09:17.660 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
There is no promise of

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.945 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
results in this lesson.

00:09:19.136 --> 00:09:20.744 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Numbers marked Example are

00:09:20.744 --> 00:09:22.421 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
teaching numbers, not advice.

00:09:23.471 --> 00:09:25.864 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper or demo trading is like driving

00:09:25.864 --> 00:09:27.948 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
with L-plates: you practise with

00:09:27.948 --> 00:09:30.417 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
pretend money before anything is real.

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:32.454 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Lesson 7 shows you how.

00:09:33.511 --> 00:09:34.638 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps one to six.

00:09:35.338 --> 00:09:37.026 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
This introduction is step one.

00:09:37.726 --> 00:09:38.787 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then what you need.

00:09:39.418 --> 00:09:40.945 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then exactly what a grid

00:09:40.945 --> 00:09:42.396 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot does, order by order.

00:09:43.395 --> 00:09:44.512 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then market regimes.

00:09:45.089 --> 00:09:47.156 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then choosing grid spacing and range.

00:09:47.795 --> 00:09:49.402 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then entry and exit rules.

00:09:50.117 --> 00:09:51.417 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Steps seven to eleven.

00:09:52.117 --> 00:09:53.201 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then a paper test.

00:09:53.922 --> 00:09:54.983 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then weekly checks.

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:56.909 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then common mistakes.

00:09:57.609 --> 00:09:59.620 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then scaling up under written rules.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:01.471 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Then an opt-in lesson on

00:10:01.471 --> 00:10:03.557 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
liquidation and your complete plan.

00:10:04.607 --> 00:10:06.506 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The next lesson is a checklist you

00:10:06.506 --> 00:10:08.406 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
write on paper, before any screen.

00:10:09.428 --> 00:10:11.805 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In short: a grid waits, it buys lower and

00:10:11.805 --> 00:10:14.182 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
sells higher while price bounces, the

00:10:14.182 --> 00:10:16.482 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
fees come out of the gap, and if a daily

00:10:16.482 --> 00:10:18.935 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves and stays out, you stop the

00:10:18.935 --> 00:10:21.005 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:22.956 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Check yourself.

00:10:23.476 --> 00:10:24.929 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Why does a grid start with

00:10:24.929 --> 00:10:26.381 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
some coin as well as cash?

00:10:26.544 --> 00:10:27.829 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Because the sell orders

00:10:27.829 --> 00:10:29.337 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
need coin you already hold.

00:10:30.355 --> 00:10:31.863 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example pair, why is

00:10:31.863 --> 00:10:33.539 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the net about eight and a half

00:10:33.539 --> 00:10:35.215 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
dollars and not the whole gap?

00:10:35.646 --> 00:10:37.210 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The two fees come out first.

00:10:38.373 --> 00:10:40.440 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Price closes above your top line, and

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:42.619 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the next day's close is still above it.

00:10:42.926 --> 00:10:44.714 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
What do you do, and who does it?

00:10:45.034 --> 00:10:46.822 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You stop the bot and follow your

00:10:46.822 --> 00:10:48.665 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
written rule, by hand, unless you

00:10:48.665 --> 00:10:50.509 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
turned on the bot's stop setting.

00:10:51.566 --> 00:10:52.316 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Your turn.

00:10:52.762 --> 00:10:54.494 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
On paper, write the top and the

00:10:54.494 --> 00:10:56.449 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
bottom, one gap, and the stop rule.

00:10:57.553 --> 00:10:59.285 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Say what you will do if a daily

00:10:59.285 --> 00:11:00.905 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
close leaves the band and the

00:11:00.905 --> 00:11:02.469 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.197 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Pause the video and write

00:11:04.197 --> 00:11:05.817 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your answer before you go on.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
No real order is sent in this lesson.

00:11:09.404 --> 00:11:11.307 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Paper practice comes in Lesson

00:11:11.307 --> 00:11:12.917 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
7, and real money only after

00:11:12.917 --> 00:11:14.747 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your written graduation rule.

00:11:15.267 --> 00:11:17.274 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A graduation rule is the written

00:11:17.274 --> 00:11:18.983 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
test you pass on paper first.

00:11:19.516 --> 00:11:20.525 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
You draw the idea.

00:11:21.045 --> 00:11:22.839 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a screen appears later, it

00:11:22.839 --> 00:11:24.554 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
should be a copy of the page,

00:11:24.554 --> 00:11:26.114 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and only on paper or demo.

00:11:27.314 --> 00:11:29.675 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring a notebook, and no secrets: no

00:11:29.675 --> 00:11:32.289 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
seed phrase, private key or API secret.

00:11:32.809 --> 00:11:34.666 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Those are the words or keys that

00:11:34.666 --> 00:11:36.380 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
unlock a wallet or an account.

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:39.122 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The pair, in the next lesson,

00:11:39.122 --> 00:11:40.737 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
is the two things you swap,

00:11:40.737 --> 00:11:42.506 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
like bitcoin and US dollars.

00:11:43.556 --> 00:11:45.390 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A grid bot places waiting buys

00:11:45.390 --> 00:11:47.443 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
below the price and waiting sells

00:11:47.443 --> 00:11:49.423 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
above it, inside a band you choose.

00:11:50.623 --> 00:11:51.740 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
A finished pair buys

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:53.025 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
lower and sells higher.

00:11:53.231 --> 00:11:54.851 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
The fees come out of the gap.

00:11:55.141 --> 00:11:57.320 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
In the example that was about eight and

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.554 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
a half dollars, and it is not a promise.

00:12:00.406 --> 00:12:01.803 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the top and

00:12:01.803 --> 00:12:02.976 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
you hold mostly cash.

00:12:03.425 --> 00:12:04.766 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Leave through the bottom

00:12:04.766 --> 00:12:06.162 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
and you hold mostly coin.

00:12:07.204 --> 00:12:09.442 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
If a daily close leaves the band and the

00:12:09.442 --> 00:12:11.539 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
next close is still outside, you stop

00:12:11.539 --> 00:12:13.662 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
the bot and follow the rule you wrote.

00:12:14.837 --> 00:12:17.072 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:19.024 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Bring your notes: your band,

00:12:19.024 --> 00:12:20.644 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
your gaps and your stop rule.

00:12:20.918 --> 00:12:22.275 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Keep the word Example on

00:12:22.275 --> 00:12:23.565 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
every practice figure.

00:12:24.085 --> 00:12:26.040 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
Next lesson you will write the page

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:28.051 line:78% position:50% align:center size:90%
of what you need, before any screen.

